$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2-Amino-4-bromo-N-(((2S*,5R*)-5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-methyl)benzamide
(rac-8b). DIPEA (1.15 mL, 6.94 mmol) and HATU (1.32 g, 3.47 mmol) was
added to the suspension of 2-amino-4-bromobenzoic acid (5) (0.5 g, 2.31
mmol) in dry DCM (20 mL), and the mixture was stirred at rt for 15 min.
Then 5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methanamine (rac -7b) (0.36 mL, 3.47
mmol) was added, and the mixture was stirred at rt for 2 h. The solvent
was then removed in vacuum, and the remaining residue was purified by
column chromatography (1/1 = EtOAc/PE),
2-Amino-4-bromo-N-(((2S*,5R*)-5-(naphthalen-2-yl)-tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methyl)benzamide
(rac-8e). Prepared in analogy to compound rac-8b. Yield 0.29 g (83%),
yellowish oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.83-1.91 (m, 1H), 1.97-2.06
(m, 1H), 2.14-2.22 (m, 1H), 2.39-2.47 (m, 1H), 3.51-3.57 (m, 1H),
3.82-3.88 (m, 1H), 4.31 (qd, J = 3.1 Hz, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 5.11 (t, J = 7.0
Hz, 1H), 5.63 (brs, 2H), 6.42 (brs, 1H), 6.57 (dd, J = 2.0 Hz, 8.2 Hz,
1H), 6.82 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.43-7.52 (m,
3H), 7.79-7.84 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 28.9, 33.7, 43.3,
78.5, 81.3, 114.4, 119.3, 119.4, 124.0, 124.4, 125.9, 126.2, 126.4,
127.6, 127.8, 128.4, 128.3, 132.9, 133.1, 139.6, 149.8, 168.7. MS (ESI)
m/z (relative intensity): 425.3 (99%), 426.3 (36.6%), 427.3 (100%), 428.3
(36.6%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
