$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A: Amide coupling reaction
for the synthesis of piperidine carboxamides 10a-i. Unless otherwise
stated, the procedures for the synthesis of the piperidine carboxamides
are as follow: To a round bottom flask was added carboxylic acid (1
equiv) and DCC or EDCI (1.05 equiv). DCM/DMF was added and the reaction
mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 30 min. To this solution was then added
respective amine or amine salt (1-2 equiv) with/without DIEA (2 equiv).
The reaction mixture was warmed up to RT and stirred overnight before
filtering over celite. The mother liquor (or reaction mixture) was washed
1x with 5% citric acid, 1x saturated NaHCO3, 1x with H2O and 1x with
brine. The washed organic mixture was then dried with Na2SO4, and
concentrated in vacuo to give a crude residue which was purified using
column chromatography (SiO2, eluent: hexane/EtOAc or DCM/MeOH). Desired
piperidine carboxamide.
N-(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)-4-(4-phenylmethyl-amidoacetyl)piperidine (10a).
N-(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)-4-(4-phenylethyl-amidoacetyl)piperidine (10b)
Carboxamide 10b was prepared following the general procedure A using
carboxylic acid 9 (1.00 g, 4.36 mmol), phenylethylamine (550 mg, 4.36
mmol) and DCC (945 mg, 4.58 mmol). After column chromatography (SiO2,
eluent: 50% hexane, 50% EtOAc). The pure carboxamide 10b was obtained in
78% yield (1.13 g). White solid. 1H NMR (400MHz; DMSO-d6) δ 1.29-1.43 (m,
2H), 1.39 (s, 9H), 1.51-1.63 (m, 2H), 2.23 (m, 1H), 2.58-2.86 (m, 2H),
2.69 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 3.21-3.29 (m, 2H), 3.83-3.98 (m, 2H), 7.14-7.33
(m, 5H), 7.86 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ 28.4, 28.6, 35.6, 40.4,
43.3, 79.5, 126.5, 128.6, 128.7, 138.8, 154.6, 174.2; ESI-MS (m/z) calcd
for C19H28N2O3 [M+H]+ 333.2; found 333.2.
